### Rewriting the radical as a rational power

$\begin{align}
h(x)&=\sqrt[3]{x^2}
\\\\
&=x^{^{\Large\frac{2}{3}}}
\end{align}$

### Differentiating using the power rule

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}h'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(x^{^{\Large\frac{2}{3}}}\right)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{3}x^{^{\Large\frac{2}{3}-1}}\qquad\gray{\text{The power rule}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2}{3}x^{^{\Large-\frac{1}{3}}}
\end{align}$
